we have been chronicling the Journey of  Survivor Rosemarie Melanson for five  years in fact she may have spent more  time in the hospital than anyone else so  as we approach this anniversary I talked  with her and her daughters about that  night in fact her pulse stopped and  she's convinced she died on the field  that night but the family has turned  that tragedy into Triumph  Rosemarie Melanson has come a long way  from this bedside interview sometimes  they're good days and  and some days the mother of four was at  the Route 91 Harvest Festival with her  daughters when she was hit by a single  armor-piercing bullet I looked up at the  sky and I saw no fireworks I knew right  away I saw my God we're in trouble I was  grabbing my mom's head and just  screaming screaming for her mom mom  and the last thing she said to me was  the last thing she said she couldn't  breathe her youngest daughter was hurt  too but in the chaos a sense of calm I  could feel my spirit actually leave and  actually it left my body and it is  literally levitating like 20 feet Over  My Dead Body I could see myself I'm  looking down  I said I could see the two girls looking  over me they're screaming and yelling I  could hear the bullets flying she was  one of the first shot and one of the  last to come home I was on life support  for two months and spent 13 months in a  hospital I took the bullet to the chest  it broke two ribs it punctured my lungs  it blew out the junction with the  esophagus meets the stomach went through  my stomach took out a third of my liver  and went through my spleen but somehow  she survived and reflected on those  moments in the light I was told when I  come back that I was to share these  words that we are to be kind we are to  be humble and that love is the key while  mom held on to a newfound mission  [Music]  her girls threw themselves into their  work at the family business Dance  Dynamics in downtown Summerlin it was  really important for our family to you  know be together and making sure we were  there for her recovery but at the same  time we knew that mom wouldn't want us  to give up on our dream and give up on  what we've worked literally our whole  lives for the business blossomed and The  Matriarch made it home more than a year  later  [Applause]  too many holidays in the hospital they  went on a cruise celebrated their  blessings in business and in life at the  annual Vegas strong 5K seeing her make  that progress makes everyone else that  much stronger because if she can do it  anyone else can do it the phrase  Melanson strong has become a family  motto whatever it is that you are  fighting you can get through it one day  at a time  and once again the family will be back  at the 5K again this weekend Rose Marie  has written a book you saw it there the  cover of it it's called beating the odds  with kindness humility hope and love  should be available for pre-sale later  this month
 

